<title>USA: Mylan says FDA approves etodolac capsules.</title>
<headline>Mylan says FDA approves etodolac capsules.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mylan Laboratories Inc said Friday  it has received an approval from the Food and Drug Administration to make and market etodolac capsules in 200mg and 300mg strengths.</p>
<p>The company said etodolac, the generic equivalent of Wyeth-Ayerst lodine, is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug for managing symptoms of osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis. It is also for managing pain.</p>
<p>The company said the product will be made in its Morgantown, W.V. manufacturing plant.</p>
<p>Shipment will begin immediately.</p>
</text>
